 "_": "Trainer key -> picture in the owner's resources/sprites/trainer sprites/ pack. build.sh embeds these; trainerURL() prefers them over the Showdown set in resources/sprites/trainer sprites/more trainers/. The games never gave the Poké Mart clerk a battle sprite, so the Mart uses Pokémon UNITE's shop clerk. The Move Reminder is the Gen 3 Expert (an old man, like FireRed/LeafGreen's Move Maniac). rg_* are the other regions' Professors, Gym Leaders, Elite Four and Champions (their Journeys are coming soon: REGIONS_SOON in a4_story.js). jo_* are the Johto Journey's people (a4b_johto.js): HeartGold/SoulSilver's pictures, Red's and Blue's FireRed/LeafGreen ones (the pack has no HeartGold/SoulSilver Red or Blue); the Kanto Gym Leaders are Crystal's trip to Kanto (chapter 10) and Johto's Battle Tower wing, the Frontier Brains the wing's. ho_* are the Hoenn Journey's people and its Battle Tower wing (a4c_hoenn.js): Game Boy Advance pictures, Emerald's for the Journey (\"GEN 3\") and Ruby/Sapphire's for their teams in the Tower (\"GEN 3 RS\"); Mom, Mr. Briney, Mr. Stone, and the Tower's Omega Ruby/Alpha Sapphire rival, Zinnia and Aarune never had one, so theirs are the pack's newer pictures. kt_* are the Battle Tower's Kanto wing (a4_story.js): Yellow's pictures (\"GEN 1\"), FireRed/LeafGreen's (\"GEN 3\"), Let's Go's (\"LGPE\"; Lt. Surge and Bruno never had one there, so theirs are the pack's newer pictures), Coach Trainers as Sun and Moon's Ace Trainers, the Master Trainers by their class. si_* are the Sinnoh Journey's people (a4d_sinnoh.js): Diamond/Pearl/Platinum's DS pictures (Platinum's \"GEN 4\" ones where the pack has both, Dawn and Lucas in their Platinum outfits); Looker, Bebe and Cynthia's grandmother never had one, so they speak without a picture. un_* are the Unova Journey's people and its Battle Tower wing (a4e_unova.js): Black/White's pictures (the pack's plain names, and \"GEN 5 BW\" for Ghetsis and the Team Plasma Grunts), Black 2/White 2's where a character changed (Cheren, Elesa, Iris, Ghetsis and Neo Team Plasma, Bianca's Pokémon World Tournament outfit); the other regions' Leaders and Champions in its wing are the pack's Black 2/White 2 Tournament pictures (Red and Blue, who have none there, FireRed/LeafGreen's). ka_* are the Kalos Journey's people and its Battle Tower wing (a4f_kalos.js): X and Y's pictures (\"GEN 6 XY\" where the pack has an Omega Ruby/Alpha Sapphire one too, the pack's plain names for the X and Y classes); Team Flare's scientists Celosia, Aliana and Mable and its Admins never got a picture in the pack, so they battle in the Team Flare Grunts' (Bryony has her own), and Looker, Gurkinn and Alexa speak without one. al_* are the Alola Journey's people and its Battle Tower wing (a4g_alola.js): Sun and Moon's and Ultra Sun and Ultra Moon's pictures (the pack's plain names for Alola's own people, \"GEN 7\" for the Gen 7 classes and the Kanto visitors, Red, Blue and Anabel; Lillie's Z-Powered outfit for her post-game; Team Rainbow Rocket's Grunts and Giovanni in their Ultra Sun and Ultra Moon outfits, Archie's \"USUM\" picture and Maxie's Omega Ruby/Alpha Sapphire one, which Ultra Sun and Ultra Moon reuse); the captainless trial at Vast Poni Canyon shows the Trial Guide. The Rotom Pokédex speaks without a picture. ga_* are the Galar Journey's people and its Battle Tower wing (a4h_galar.js): Sword and Shield's pictures (the pack's plain names for Galar's own people and \"GEN 8\" for the Gen 8 classes; Leon's Battle Tower outfit for its floors, Marnie's and Bede's Champion Cup ones, Rose's holiday clothes in Hulbury, Sonia's lab coat once she's a professor); the Gym Trainers, who have no picture in the pack, battle in the League Staff's, and Macro Cosmos's staff in the Office Worker's. Honey, Hyde, Calyrex, the Rotom Phone and Cara Liss speak without one (Honey's battle is left out). pa_* are the Paldea Journey's people and its Battle Tower wing (a4i_paldea.js): Scarlet's pictures where the pack has both versions (Nemona's and Arven's Naranja Academy uniforms, Clavell's Scarlet suit; Clive's disguise is the pack's one, Violet's), the pack's plain names for Paldea's own people and the DLC's, and \"GEN 9\" for the Gen 9 classes; the Academy's Students, who have no picture in the pack, are its Gen 8 schoolkids in uniform. Snacksworth and the Kitakami villagers speak without a picture.",
